================================================================================
IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS
================================================================================

AsyncTaskRouter Structure:
  - queue_tx: mpsc::Sender<MandateTask>
  - queue_size_limit: usize (bounded capacity)
  - worker_count: u32 (worker fleet size)
  - circuit_breaker_state: Arc<Mutex<CircuitBreakerState>>
  - connection_pool_limit: Arc<Semaphore> (concurrent execution bound)

Worker Loop Logic:
  1. recv() from channel (blocks until task available)
  2. Acquire semaphore permit (blocks until available)
  3. Process task (1ms simulated work)
  4. Permit released on scope exit
  5. Loop continues until channel closes

Backpressure Chain:
  1. Queue full (10k tasks) → try_send() fails
  2. Caller receives CapacityExhausted (HTTP 429 semantics)
  3. Caller must retry or fail-closed

Connection Pool Enforcement:
  - Semaphore initialized to max_concurrent = max(5, worker_count/2)
  - For 8 workers: max_concurrent = max(5, 4) = 5 permits
  - Each worker acquires permit before processing
  - At most 5 tasks execute concurrently (enforced)
  - Excess tasks queued waiting for available permit

