Test: test_connection_pool_exhaustion_graceful_degradation

Code Structure:
  let router = AsyncTaskRouter::new(100, 8).await;  // Created but NOT USED
  for i in 0..50 {
    tokio::spawn(async move {                        // Independent tasks
      let conn_count = active.fetch_add(1, ...);    // Increment counter
      tokio::time::sleep(10ms).await;               // Simulate DB query
      active.fetch_sub(1, ...);                     // Decrement counter
    });
  }

Expected Behavior (per test):
  - Max concurrent ≤ 15 (5 connection limit + 10 buffer)

Actual Behavior:
  - Max concurrent = 50 (all tasks active nearly simultaneously)
  
Why Mismatch:
  - Tasks do NOT call router.submit_task()
  - Router's semaphore does NOT apply to independent spawned tasks
  - Tokio can run thousands of concurrent lightweight tasks
  - 50 tasks with 10ms sleep = ~50 concurrent within time window

Resolution Options:
  A. Modify test to submit tasks through router
  B. Implement global tokio task limiting (not possible)
  C. Accept as known limitation of current test design
  D. Escalate for Sonnet diagnostics on concurrency patterns

Recommended: Option D (user guidance on test intent)

